{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01M1FiisoKYZa1hXYP5hcHDK","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t//go:build bdd\n2\t\n3\t// Package steps holds the step definitions for the `mcp` test suite.\n4\t//\n5\t// The suite is resolved from docs/architecture/architecture.yaml: service\n6\t// `mcp-service` owns the tests/mcp tree, so every definition the mcp\n7\t// scenarios bind to lives in this package and is registered from the one\n8\t// Register call below.\n9\tpackage steps\n10\t\n11\timport (\n12\t\t\"bytes\"\n13\t\t\"encoding/json\"\n14\t\t\"fmt\"\n15\t\t\"io\"\n16\t\t\"net\"\n17\t\t\"net/http\"\n18\t\t\"os\"\n19\t\t\"strconv\"\n20\t\t\"strings\"\n21\t\t\"time\"\n22\t)\n23\t\n24\t// StepFunc is the shape of every step definition in this package: it\n25\t// receives the pattern's capture groups in order and reports failure as an\n26\t// error, because that error IS the test failure a reader gets.\n27\ttype StepFunc func(args ...string) error\n28\t\n29\t// Suite is the seam the suite runner satisfies. It is declared here rather\n30\t// than imported so this package carries no dependency on the runner, which\n31\t// lets the runner import these definitions and call Register without an\n32\t// import cycle.\n33\ttype Suite interface {\n34\t\tStep(pattern string, fn StepFunc)\n35\t}\n36\t\n37\tconst (\n38\t\t// defaultPort is the configured MCP port when the environment is silent.\n39\t\tdefaultPort = 8080\n40\t\t// portEnvVar overrides defaultPort for a run.\n41\t\tportEnvVar = \"MCP_PORT\"\n42\t\n43\t\tdialTimeout  = 2 * time.Second\n44\t\thttpTimeout  = 10 * time.Second\n45\t\tmaxBodyBytes = 64 << 10\n46\t\n47\t\t// protocolVersion is the MCP revision the suite advertises when it\n48\t\t// initializes, so the request the When step sends is a valid one.\n49\t\tprotocolVersion = \"2025-06-18\"\n50\t)\n51\t\n52\t// State is the single piece of mutable state the mcp step definitions\n53\t// share: a Given fills in the server coordinates,